From: ParticleVE maintainers
Subject: Report the expected SBOM linker choice as an informational message

The build deliberately enables uSWID. Selecting the bundled linker script is
the required successful path for retaining .sbom, rather than an error. Keep
all compiler warnings fatal and verify the emitted .sbom and .sbat sections in
the RPM check phase. This changes only this one configuration diagnostic.

--- a/efi/meson.build
+++ b/efi/meson.build
@@ -110,6 +110,6 @@
 # SBOM is never in system lds
 if uswid.found()
-  warning('Switching to local copy of linker script as using SBOM')
+  message('Using bundled linker script to retain the SBOM section')
   efi_ldsdir = join_paths(meson.current_source_dir(), 'lds')
   arch_lds = 'elf_@0@@1@_efi.lds'.format(gnu_efi_arch, lds_os)
 endif
